{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 6: The Mood Ring",
  "description": "See how neural networks map text to continuous affect!\n\nThis network converts words into a 5-DIMENSIONAL AFFECT SPACE:\n- Valence: Pleasure (-1 to +1)\n- Arousal: Energy level (0 to 1)\n- Dominance: Control (0 to 1)\n- Sorrow: Sadness (0 to 1)\n- Boredom: Disinterest (0 to 1)\n\nWHY CONTINUOUS AFFECT?\nDiscrete emotion labels (happy, sad, angry) are too simple.\nReal feelings blend and shift continuously.\n\nTRY THESE WORDS:\n- happy, joy, love -> High valence, moderate arousal\n- sad, crying, grief -> Low valence, high sorrow\n- angry, furious, rage -> Low valence, HIGH arousal\n- calm, peaceful, serene -> Neutral valence, LOW arousal\n- bored, tedious, dull -> High boredom\n\nTHIS IS THE NOODLINGS AFFECT MODEL!\nEvery noodling's emotional state lives in this 5D space.",
  "metadata": {
